     "<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt;word-wrap:break-word\">Dear all,</p><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:georgia\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">We would like to inform you that only 1 seat available for our upcoming Physalia online course: Phylogenetic Comparative Methods in R.</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"><br>Dates: 12–16 May </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">Course website: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course44/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course44/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483215508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FWm2Juq5oeGPRQAW0ehT0\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course44/</a></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the use of ultrametric phylogenies in trait evolution and lineage diversification studies. Designed for researchers and students with a background in molecular evolution and some familiarity with R, the course combines theoretical lectures with hands-on practical sessions.</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">For the full list of our courses and workshops, please visit: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course44/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course44/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483215508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FWm2Juq5oeGPRQAW0ehT0\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/</a></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">Best regards,</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">Carlo</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:verdana;font-size:10pt;word-wrap:break-word\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;;font-size:10pt\">--------------------<br><br>Carlo Pecoraro, Ph.D<br><br><br>Physalia-courses DIRECTOR<br><br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">in...@physalia-courses.org</a><br><br>mobile: <a href=\"tel:+49%20176%2045230846\" value=\"+4917645230846\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+49 17645230846</a><br><br><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/physaliacourses.bsky.social\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bsky.app/profile/physaliacourses.bsky.social&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483215508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hphyW4zk2EMHO7Fcj51ez\">Bluesky</a> <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/physalia-courses-a64418127/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.linkedin.com/in/physalia-courses-a64418127/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483215508000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2CvpO2z6iGeIX_l2wCbxVD\">Linkedin</a><br><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:10pt;word-wrap:break-word\"> </p></div></div></div>"
